\newlabel{tab:headsizes}{{III}{4}{Head size in terms of the grid it resolves densely. $N=10$ at $L=10$ holds $5$ of the $10$ bits of each axis, i.e.\ a $32\times 32$ coarse grid, with the remaining $32\times 32$ cells inside each block carried by the tail}{table.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Head cost under both normalisations, and the rate--distortion curves from which the optimum is read. Left: share of the compressed state held by the head. Centre: head size as a fraction of the dense field, which falls with $L$ at fixed $N-L$. Right: $L_2$ error against compression ratio $\rho $ for every run; $L=10$ drawn solid.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:headbudget}{{3}{5}{Head cost under both normalisations, and the rate--distortion curves from which the optimum is read. Left: share of the compressed state held by the head. Centre: head size as a fraction of the dense field, which falls with $L$ at fixed $N-L$. Right: $L_2$ error against compression ratio $\rho $ for every run; $L=10$ drawn solid}{figure.3}{}}
